  "body": "The gate is green. This PR waits for an independent review; it stays a draft until then.\n\n## What changed\n\nLaw (c)'s island membership test no longer scans the whole cached slice on\nevery point query. `Rest::island_holds` now asks an exact Y-slab point index\n(`crates/sim/src/verify/slice_index.rs`). The index keeps every cut plane and\nevery sample; it reads only the edges whose Y span holds the query point, and\nit computes the crossing with the same expression, in the same order, as\n`Region::contains`, so the answer is bit for bit.\n\nThe rejected levels-plus-deepest plane set is removed:\n`crates/sim/src/verify/cut_planes.rs` is deleted, and `reach.rs` and `mod.rs`\nare back on main's plane loop (`rest.cut()`, one slice per cut plane).\n\nFiles:\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/slice_index.rs` (new: index and its direct pin)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/rest.rs` (cache holds `Rc<IndexedSlice>`)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/reach_tests.rs` (stepped fixture, model-parameterized compare)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/mod.rs` (module)\n- `docs/decisions/3615-verify-cut-levels.md` (accepted design)\n\n## Equivalence\n\n`verify::reach_tests::a_many_plane_ramp_reads_only_the_samples_near_its_discs`\ncompares law (c) with the all-plane reference (`reach_reference`) and fails if\nany finding, its order, or the slice count moves.\n\n- Sloped ramp `ramp_at(500, 36.0)`: equal findings; `slices 500 == 500`;\n  `sample_tests 20,192` new vs `1,394,117` reference.\n- Stepped fixture (wide low block under a narrow tall block) at Y 49: equal\n  findings; `slices 500 == 500`; `sample_tests 28,368` vs `1,390,052`.\n- Away-from-wall ramp `ramp_at(500, 34)`: equal findings; `sample_tests 0`\n  vs `2,004,000`.\n\nThe stepped fixture exposes the levels-only failure: on a temporary variant\nthat keeps only the wide low block (the deepest section's sample set), the\nreference convicts 93 `ShankHit { part: true }` moves and the wide-only set\nconvicts 63, losing moves 250 to 279 (30 part-true). The narrow band's Y 45\nwall sample is what catches them.\n\nThe index itself is pinned directly: `verify::slice_index::tests::the_index_equals_region_contains_bit_for_bit`\ncompares it with `Region::contains` over a grid that lands on every vertex\nline and between them, for a U, a staircase and a holed region.\n\n## Gates run\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim --lib verify::`: 160 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base 65b52cca6 --only \"app heavy: verify\"`: ok in\n  450 s (`--release --ignored`, the sim verify heavy lane).\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base 65b52cca6`: not run. Its three twins are the\n  motion slot, motion trochoidal and app pocket-pass-start lanes, none of\n  which read the verifier; the light build links every motion and app test\n  binary in release, a cut-level cost.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full mechanical heavy reach (`app heavy: every target`, `motion heavy:\n  every target`) is a cut-level run; the sim verify heavy coverage is the\n  `app heavy: verify` lane.\n- The real #3577 fig8 path: the counterexamples are the sloped and stepped\n  fixtures.\n\nChangelog: none (perf, no behaviour change)\n\nEffort: max\nFixes #3615\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
